# What `docker build` must not send to the daemon as build context. Two of
# these entries are correctness, not speed, and both are about Dockerfile.api.
#
# ui/node_modules -- Dockerfile.api installs the UI's dependencies inside
# node:24 (COPY package.json + package-lock.json, RUN npm ci) and only then
# copies the rest of ui/ over the result. Without this line that second COPY
# replaces the tree npm ci just built with whatever the host has, which on a
# machine where `make ui` has run means esbuild's and rolldown's
# platform-specific binaries from the host's OS and architecture. On a
# non-linux/amd64 host that fails the build outright; everywhere it defeats
# the package.json-first layer split, whose whole point is that a source
# change does not reinstall the dependency tree. CI has only ever passed
# because a fresh checkout has no node_modules to send.
#
# webui/dist -- the Go stage does `COPY . .` and then
# `COPY --from=ui /webui/dist ./webui/dist`, and a COPY into an existing
# directory MERGES rather than replaces. So the host's last local build
# would survive into the image beside the fresh one: content-hashed assets
# from an older bundle, referenced by nothing, embedded in the binary and
# shipped. Excluding it means the directory the ui stage produces is the
# only one there is.
#
# The pattern excludes the build output but not webui/dist/.gitkeep, and
# that exception is load-bearing rather than tidiness: webui/webui.go's
# //go:embed all:dist fails to COMPILE, not merely to run, against a
# directory that does not exist, and .gitkeep is the only thing that keeps
# the directory present -- and go build ./... working -- on a checkout
# where Node was never installed. Dockerfile.api's ui stage always repopulates
# the directory before the Go stage's COPY above, so the negation costs
# nothing here; it is what keeps a future build context (a Dockerfile for
# cmd/vantage, or a go vet ./... step) from failing on a directory this
# entry deleted for no reason of its own.
ui/node_modules
**/node_modules
webui/dist/*
!webui/dist/.gitkeep

# Private keys and local state, below this line. The Go stages do
# `COPY . .`, so anything left in the context is in a build layer -- visible
# to anyone with the build cache or a `docker history` of an intermediate
# image, even though no final stage copies it. These mirror .gitignore's
# entries for material that is local or secret; no Dockerfile here reads any
# of them.
#
# gen-certs.sh output (CA and client private keys, and the Secrets carrying
# them in the clear) at any depth. The whole directory rather than the
# .gitignore's per-file patterns: git needs deploy/nats-tls/gen-certs.sh
# tracked, but no image build needs the script either.
**/nats-tls
.tls/
# Agent, editor and browser-tool scratch: session notes, ledgers, page
# snapshots. Local to one machine and never source.
.superpowers/
.remember/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/
.idea/
.worktrees/
# The fetched RIPE AS-name data (about 12 MiB); the ClickHouse host reads
# it, not any image.
deploy/dev/asnames/
# Lab state: containerlab's root-owned per-lab directories, CML lab ids,
# router captures and capture logs. No image imports anything under lab/.
lab/
__pycache__/

# Size only, below this line. Nothing in any Dockerfile here reads either --
# no build embeds a git revision, and bin/ holds host-built binaries the Go
# stage recompiles from source anyway.
.git
bin
